# Fiscal provider layer (do not regress)

POS flows call fiscalization only via `services/fiscal` (`loadFiscalContext`, `provider.*`, `wrapFiscalError`, `resolvePendingFiscalProvider`) — same layer in `web-frontend` and `restaurant-frontend`.

Restaurant callers: `restaurant/pos/utils/payRestaurantOrderWithFiscal.js`, `restaurant/pos/utils/pendingFiscalQueue.js` (restaurant provider also exposes `resolveErrorMessage`).

## Invariants

1. `posDataRouter` (shift open/close/X, sale), `posReturnWithFiscal`, `offlineSyncService` must not import fiscal operations from `services/multikassa` directly. POS loads caps via `loadFiscalCapabilities` → `GET /cashier/fiscal`. `/cashier/multikassa` is Multikassa UI/flags only and must not return FiscalDrive `factoryId` / FD `enabled`. Pay rail has no fiscal switches. **FiscalDrive is hidden from cashier and admin cash-register UI for now** — `GET /cashier/fiscal` always returns Multikassa. Do not remount FD menu/settings until the user asks to bring it back.
2. Missing/unknown `capabilities.fiscalProvider` or `payload.fiscal.fiscalProvider` → **Multikassa**. Existing client registers must keep working unchanged.
3. Multikassa stays a supported provider for live clients — do not delete or rewrite it while adding FiscalDrive. When `fiscal_provider=MULTIKASSA`, sale/shift/QR/`requireBeforeSale` stay on the Multikassa path (`services/multikassa/*`, localhost:8080 / mkfiscal). Do not open FiscalDrive Z, List FactoryID, or RegisterTXID on a Multikassa register.
4. A new provider = new file in `services/fiscal/providers/` + entry in `resolveFiscalProvider`; no `if (provider === ...)` in POS flows.
5. Error codes surfaced to UI (`MULTIKASSA_*`) stay as-is for the Multikassa provider.
6. Provider-neutral helpers live in `services/fiscal` (`fiscalStatus`, `shared/toSaleFiscalPayload`, `shared/ofdMarkingLabel`, `shared/resolveFiscalPackageCodes`, `shared/expandMarkedFiscalItems`). Providers import them from there; `services/fiscal/shared` must never import from `services/multikassa`.
7. Backend source of truth: `cash_registers.fiscal_provider` (`FiscalProvider` enum, default `MULTIKASSA`, Liquibase v46). It is per cash register (not in the Multikassa settings table) and is returned as `fiscalProvider` in cashier capabilities and admin settings, even when Multikassa is disabled.
8. FiscalDrive connection settings live in `cash_register_fiscal_drive_settings` (v47, `/admin/cash-registers/{id}/fiscal-drive`). Calls to the local FiscalDriveService go through `fiscal/shared/localDeviceHttp.js` → Electron `desktop:localDeviceRequest`, which must stay **loopback-only** (do not widen it to arbitrary hosts; Multikassa cloud keeps its own proxy).
9. Marking check before a FiscalDrive receipt: frontend `validateFiscalMarking` → backend `POST /cashier/marking/validate` → tax `validation-onkm`. Credentials only in env `MARKING_VALIDATION_USERNAME/PASSWORD` (never in yml defaults, code, or frontend). `ownerTin`/`terminalId` come from the register's FiscalDrive settings, not from the client. Network/auth failures return `UNAVAILABLE` (not 500); `REJECTED` carries the tax code (1001…2090). This is separate from the Asl Belgisi integration — do not merge them.
10. FiscalDrive sale path: `GetTXID` → `RegisterTXID` (retry on link failure; store TXID for pending). Capabilities for `FISCAL_DRIVE` come from `cash_register_fiscal_drive_settings` (not Multikassa enabled flag). Switch provider only via FiscalDrive settings `useForFiscalization` — default stays Multikassa. Refund via FiscalDrive is not ready yet.
11. FiscalDrive (`fiscal_provider=FISCAL_DRIVE`) never completes a sale without RegisterTXID proof (`FiscalSign` + `QRCodeURL` on ofd.soliq.uz). Do not inherit Multikassa `requireBeforeSale` / `printFiscalQr` into FD capabilities. Before GetTXID: List FactoryID if missing, `State/Sync` if Locked, `ZReport/Open` if Z is closed. On 0x9021 retry RegisterTXID with the **same** TXID (never GetTXID again for that receipt). Type «Покупка» on the sale is not fiscal proof. Receipt `Time` must be `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS` (never empty). Do not send `RefundInfo.DateTime=""`. GetTXID form `JsonReceipt` that returns empty-DateTime 500 must retry the same receipt as raw JSON once — that is not a second sale. Other POS (SmartPOS/E-POS) only see the KM as sold after OFD gets Labels from RegisterTXID.
